{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 30,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " younger than I, have me in derision, whose fathers I would have disdained to set with the dogs of my flock.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, to what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "might",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the strength of their hands ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "profit",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " me, in whom old age had perished?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For want and famine ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " solitary; fleeing into the wilderness in former time desolate and waste.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who cut up mallows by the bushes, and juniper roots ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They were driven forth from among ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", (they cried after them, as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "after",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a thief;)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To dwell in the clefts of the valleys, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " caves of the earth, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the rocks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Among the bushes they brayed; under the nettles they were collected.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " children of fools, yes, children of base men: they were viler than the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now I am their song, yes, I am their by-word.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They abhor me, they flee far from me, and spare not to spit in my face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because he hath loosed my cord, and afflicted me, they have also let loose the bridle before me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Upon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " right ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "hand",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rise the youth; they push away my feet, and they raise up against me the ways of their destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They mar my path, they set forward my calamity, they have no helper.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They came ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "upon me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a wide breaking in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of waters",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": in the desolation they rolled themselves ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "upon me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Terrors are turned upon me: they pursue my soul as the wind: and my welfare passeth away as a cloud.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now my soul is poured out upon me; the days of affliction have taken hold upon me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My bones are pierced in me in the night season: and my sinews take no rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By the great force ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of my disease",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is my garment changed: it bindeth me about as the collar of my coat.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath cast me into the mire, and I have become like dust and ashes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I cry to thee, and thou dost not hear me: I stand up, and thou regardest me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "not",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast become cruel to me: with thy strong hand thou opposest thyself against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou liftest me up to the wind; thou causest me to ride ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "upon it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and dissolvest my substance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou wilt bring me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " death, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the house appointed for all living.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet he will not stretch out ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hand to the grave, though they cry in his destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Did not I weep for him that was in trouble? was ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "not",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my soul grieved for the poor?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I looked for good, then evil came: and when I waited for light, there came darkness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My bowels boiled, and rested not: the days of affliction came upon me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I went mourning without the sun: I stood up, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I cried in the congregation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am a brother to dragons, and a companion to owls.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My skin is black upon me, and my bones are burned with heat.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.30.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.30.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My harp also is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "turned",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to mourning, and my organ into the voice of them that weep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
